4 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645652} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e4ec5d0-d623-5e2b-b7fc-7ae557a8d40c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{uv}+uv{e}^{uv}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645162} {:answer/id #uuid "9d60547f-15eb-549a-8336-913b7652e054" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "uv{e}^{uv}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645411} {:answer/id #uuid "e1f4a6ed-4201-5415-8ed9-0304a7c8e5ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u{e}^{uv}-2v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e4ec5d0-d623-5e2b-b7fc-7ae557a8d40c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{uv}+uv{e}^{uv}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645162} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2a182bd-4c42-5f66-8c00-aaea6da78636" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645666}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "44302ba2-4938-5ba2-b36a-49c85314e88e" :question/math-academy-id "q-318600" :question/problem "Determine whether the following differential equation is exact:\n\n$$\n(3+v{e}^{uv})\\,\\text{d}u+(u{e}^{uv}-2v)\\,\\text{d}v=0\n$$\n\nA differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u+Q(u,v)\\,\\text{d}v=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it satisfies the condition\n\n$$\n\\,{{field-1}},\n$$\n\nFor the equation $(3+v{e}^{uv})\\,\\text{d}u+(u{e}^{uv}-2v)\\,\\text{d}v=0$, we have  \n\n$$\nP=\\,{{field-2}},\n$$\n\n$$\nQ=\\,{{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂v}=\\,{{field-4}},\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂u}=\\,{{field-5}}.\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n\\,{{field-6}},\n$$\n\n the equation {{field-7}}." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u+Q(u,v)\\,\\text{d}v=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂v}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂u}.\n$$\n\nFor the equation $(3+v{e}^{uv})\\,\\text{d}u+(u{e}^{uv}-2v)\\,\\text{d}v=0$, we have  \n\n$$\nP(u,v)=3+v{e}^{uv},\\,Q(u,v)=u{e}^{uv}-2v.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂v} & =\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3+v{e}^{uv}) \\\\  & ={e}^{uv}+uv{e}^{uv},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂u} & =\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u{e}^{uv}-2v) \\\\  & ={e}^{uv}+uv{e}^{uv}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂v}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂u},\n$$\n\nthe exactness condition is satisfied. Therefore, the given differential equation $\\text{is exact}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186645711 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "238a9123-ab9e-5c21-b22f-a76f63943a54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{2})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}+1)+x=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645198} {:answer/id #uuid "67aae9a8-957c-5c2b-ab3c-721222f8e86b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}-xy=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645320} {:answer/id #uuid "83cfcb66-57cc-5b14-a0d5-57365a9aaf79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}y}{2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645368} {:answer/id #uuid "ebd99475-b8ad-5a18-8bee-dda10a96ed6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645550} {:answer/id #uuid "ec9085cf-45f6-5ceb-bbe2-d0d6ff5d704c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy+1)=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645554}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83cfcb66-57cc-5b14-a0d5-57365a9aaf79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}y}{2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645368} :answer-field/id #uuid "fef9f4c7-d6f1-5ee7-8220-1cee9a548cc7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645685}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "452f05cb-a4b1-5ca8-af67-674989ff7ee9" :question/math-academy-id "q-64220" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the differential equation\n\n$$\n(\\frac{1}{x}+xy)\\text{d}x+(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\text{d}y=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the differential equation is of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x,y)=\\frac{1}{x}+xy$ and $Q(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.$\n\nLet's check if the equation is exact. To do this, we check to see if it passes the exactness test, i.e.:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's differentiate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{1}{x}+xy)=x\n$$\n\nNow, let's differentiate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=x=\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\,✓\n$$\n\nSo, the given equation is exact and its solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=P(x,y),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{x}+xy)\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{{x}^{2}y}{2}+f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}y}{2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,\\,f(y)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}y}{2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x=c.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186645719 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16c5fd09-699d-518c-8b23-fbd0c66770cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}{y}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{11}{2}{x}^{2}+18x=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645177} {:answer/id #uuid "2828eab5-9e3c-51cc-a69a-139062dd8131" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{x}^{3}{y}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{11}{2}{y}^{2}+18x=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645206} {:answer/id #uuid "471f116a-e52d-5dd4-8dd5-964eaebb32d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}{y}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{11}{2}{y}^{2}+18x=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645259} {:answer/id #uuid "d4d0b48b-3ee9-5088-aa6a-9edcf2ccf1a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}{y}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{11}{2}{y}^{2}+18y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645517} {:answer/id #uuid "ea67d1e6-2523-54ff-9eec-f582d2484687" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}{y}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{11}{2}{y}^{2}-18x=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645547}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "471f116a-e52d-5dd4-8dd5-964eaebb32d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}{y}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{11}{2}{y}^{2}+18x=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645259} :answer-field/id #uuid "9aa785f9-9658-50db-8bd7-fbf037313ed9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645642}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "52a30f2f-3404-5735-98d7-cbccf6e23c7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-320576" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{3}+18}{\\,11y-{x}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We start by rewriting this equation in differential form.\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nStarting from \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{3}+18}{\\,11y-{x}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe first multiply through by $(11y-{x}^{3}{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x$:\n\n$$\n(11y-{x}^{3}{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y=({x}^{2}{y}^{3}+18)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we rearrange the terms:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}{y}^{3}+18)\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{3}{y}^{2}-11y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nNow, we should check for exactness. A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nFor our differential equation, we have\n\n$$\nP(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{3}+18,\\,Q(x,y)={x}^{3}{y}^{2}-11y.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\,({x}^{2}{y}^{3}+18) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}{y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\,({x}^{3}{y}^{2}-11y) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\\,✓\n$$\n\n \nThus, our equation is exact.\n\nSince the equation is exact, our solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=P(x,y),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=Q(x,y).\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int ({x}^{2}{y}^{3}+18)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}{y}^{3}}{3}+18x+f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int ({x}^{3}{y}^{2}-11y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}{y}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{11}{2}{y}^{2}+g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x)=18x,\\,f(y)=-\\frac{11}{2}{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}{y}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{11}{2}{y}^{2}+18x=c.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186645746 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e041419-afbf-5468-a489-d830c79e7aa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645189} {:answer/id #uuid "226bb6f7-8757-561b-9241-b40379e72aea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645195} {:answer/id #uuid "53d86c88-f32c-5d5f-82d7-66fb54b76717" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645284} {:answer/id #uuid "843aeac1-dc3c-51d4-a0ec-606a388c0f73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645369} {:answer/id #uuid "bd54d7d4-3b81-5bfa-8256-59b9f5adf6ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "226bb6f7-8757-561b-9241-b40379e72aea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645195} :answer-field/id #uuid "41d530c8-1299-5bb8-8941-18858bfde2be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645598}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "aa96d343-51d0-5cbd-82b3-04d57e518462" :question/math-academy-id "q-103176" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation:\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+(2{x}^{2}y-{x}^{2})\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation is exact, which of the following functions could be $P(x,y)?$\n\nI. $2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-x{y}^{2}$\n\nII. $2x{y}^{2}-2xy$\n\nIII. ${y}^{2}-x$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're given $Q(x,y)=2{x}^{2}y-{x}^{2}.$ \n\nFirst, let's differentiate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}y-{x}^{2})=4xy-2x\n$$\n\nNow, let's apply $\\frac{∂}{∂y}$ to each of the given options:\n\n- First, we check $P(x,y)=2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-x{y}^{2}.$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-x{y}^{2}) &=4{x}^{2}y-2xy\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-x{y}^{2}$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\n- Next, we check $P(x,y)=2x{y}^{2}-2xy$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{y}^{2}-2xy) &=4xy-2x=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=2x{y}^{2}-2xy$ gives an exact equation.\n\n- Finally, we check $P(x,y)={y}^{2}-x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}-x) &=2y\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)={y}^{2}-x$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\nHence, the correct answer is ''II only''."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186645751 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47ec472a-73d7-559a-9dbe-7da517090246" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)-y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645262} {:answer/id #uuid "5ce92976-4318-5125-9abe-6d6c9f069694" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{ln}^{2}⁡(xy)-y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645298} {:answer/id #uuid "5fb99d65-8732-59e6-a3a4-f294f259d390" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xy\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)-xy=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645304} {:answer/id #uuid "617be915-01bc-5ea9-ba3b-d0943acc4cdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)-x=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645308} {:answer/id #uuid "9241f64c-e6bf-57d3-962d-5c9aeda32ace" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)-xy=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47ec472a-73d7-559a-9dbe-7da517090246" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)-y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645262} :answer-field/id #uuid "0725ade2-d605-5e88-ae88-5bf77bb190b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645581}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b71ba9d0-9d3a-5d87-b5f6-2982f8e84e04" :question/math-academy-id "q-103342" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the exact differential equation\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+1)\\text{d}x+(\\frac{x}{y}-1)\\text{d}y=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the differential equation is of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+1$ and $Q(x,y)=\\frac{x}{y}-1.$\n\nSince the equation is exact, our solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=P(x,y),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+1)\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)-x+x+f(y) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+f(y) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{x}{y}-1)\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-y+g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,\\,f(y)=-y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-y & =0 \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)-y & =c\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186645758 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f5700cb-22af-5afc-ae72-fef1079d779b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{ }2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645276} {:answer/id #uuid "6556b028-7fc0-57bc-8123-c9ef4f4c6cda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645314} {:answer/id #uuid "aa4a59b7-4266-54ce-ae73-638720254d01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{ }\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645432} {:answer/id #uuid "dcc75f01-f4e0-5765-8906-5dab55a5de77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{ }-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645523}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6556b028-7fc0-57bc-8123-c9ef4f4c6cda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/