field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9146f54a-3dc1-5286-acc6-392fafa90aa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645389} :answer-field/id #uuid "d665d76f-45e5-50f4-96a2-cf0ca5631633" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645669} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74df66d5-3900-5f8c-bc3c-d6a7e229c018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "is exact" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645338} {:answer/id #uuid "c88f9831-2daa-562c-8fe3-8790e3f13f1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "is not  exact" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c88f9831-2daa-562c-8fe3-8790e3f13f1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "is not  exact" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645496} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbde6634-d430-5163-a9ea-a53987947b6b" :answer-field/key "field-7" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c9a2d30e-fa4a-5546-b768-53466672b651" :question/math-academy-id "q-320541" :question/problem "Determine whether the following differential equation is exact:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nA differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it satisfies the condition\n\n$$\n\\,{{field-1}},\n$$\n\nFor the equation $({x}^{2}+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y=0$, we have  \n\n$$\nP=\\,{{field-2}},\n$$\n\n$$\nQ=\\,{{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\,{{field-4}},\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\,{{field-5}}.\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n\\,{{field-6}},\n$$\n\n the equation {{field-7}}." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nFor the equation $({x}^{2}+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y=0$, we have \n\n$$\nP(x,y)={x}^{2}+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,Q(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, compute the partial derivatives carefully:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\,({x}^{2}+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\,(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x},\n$$\n\nso the exactness condition fails. Therefore, the given differential equation $\\text{is not exact}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186656242 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3077934f-4ae8-559c-949c-38266b1c7179" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655760} {:answer/id #uuid "bb87fe9e-b915-40ae-b5e5-d1bf84403a34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3077934f-4ae8-559c-949c-38266b1c7179" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655760} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f50ebc1-98b8-52b9-a35b-ad44762f7d30" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186656077}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c81ffd36-bea6-5ee2-b2ae-d817e775302e" :question/math-academy-id "q-349602" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}6{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$  \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=-2x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2\\,⟹\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get the following:\n\n| $x$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ | $-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡6$ |\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}6{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =6{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}{e}^{u}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-3{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{-2})}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({6}^{-2})}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {e}^{u}\\,{|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{-2})}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({6}^{-2})} \\\\  & =-3({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({6}^{-2})}-{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{-2})}) \\\\  & =-3({6}^{-2}-{3}^{-2}) \\\\  & =-3(\\frac{1}{36}-\\frac{1}{9}) \\\\  & =-3\\left(-\\frac{3}{36}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186656251 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a02956c2-5c40-5cfe-82e8-08f851f4bc7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{6}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a02956c2-5c40-5cfe-82e8-08f851f4bc7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{6}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655918} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2119313-40d0-553f-adbd-e5bcb0543879" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186656149}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f0eae6a1-741d-5ac1-a3c3-9709c1992e64" :question/math-academy-id "q-349600" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{1}6{e}^{6x}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$  \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=6x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{6}\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get the following:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $6$ |\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}6{e}^{6x}\\,\\text{d}x & =6{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{6x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{0}^{6}{e}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{6}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\,{|}_{0}^{6} \\\\  & ={e}^{6}-{e}^{0} \\\\  & ={e}^{6}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186657591 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0efedf7e-3d47-5ff8-8014-af7d7f1c524c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6^{x} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657588}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0efedf7e-3d47-5ff8-8014-af7d7f1c524c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6^{x} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657588} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd6980db-63b9-58a9-a161-58fba5aeb424" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657603}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "50d8c6ab-86f9-5697-89f9-f6bea58cd673" :question/problem "Differentiate ${6}^{x}\\sin(x).$\n\n$(6^{x} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})'=$ $6^{x} \\ln{\\left(6 \\right)} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\,+$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=6^{x}$ and $v(x)=\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(x)v(x))' &=u'(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot v'(x) \\\\ &=(6^{x})'\\cdot (\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &\\quad +(6^{x})\\cdot (\\sin{\\left(x \\right)})' \\\\ &=(6^{x} \\ln{\\left(6 \\right)})(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &\\quad +(6^{x})(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &=6^{x} \\ln{\\left(6 \\right)} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} \\\\ &\\quad +(6^{x} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186657592 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c2a69dd-025f-5be8-980e-f66236939db9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 e^{x} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 2 e^{x} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657589} {:answer/id #uuid "73eeb177-fa56-5e28-88c3-c06d587a93db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 e^{x} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657593} {:answer/id #uuid "8380cb0c-f99b-5edc-8bcb-df0b4edd19ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 e^{x} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657596} {:answer/id #uuid "91824e3e-fce8-5d21-847f-ffd4ce485006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 e^{x} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - 2 e^{x} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657598} {:answer/id #uuid "eee2ca73-2f04-51ce-9964-2aff5fa07bd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 e^{x} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - 2 e^{x} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657606}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id 